    "proxy_feature_limitation": {
      "statement": "The primary clinical features (UPDRS, MoCA, FunctionalAssessment, Tremor, Bradykinesia, Rigidity) are standardized clinical rating scales and clinician-evaluated motor signs already employed in Parkinson's clinical diagnostic evaluations, rather than independent molecular, genetic, or biofluid biomarkers (such as DaTscan or CSF alpha-synuclein). The model functions as an algorithmic clinical decision-support and risk-quantification system rather than a de novo biological discovery tool.",
